WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:02.117
The Frightened Lion

00:00:03.382 --> 00:00:06.956
(A version of the tale by TheFableCottage.com)

00:00:08.214 --> 00:00:11.547
One night, Lion is getting ready for bed.

00:00:12.084 --> 00:00:14.763
He reads his favorite bedtime story

00:00:14.763 --> 00:00:17.743
and sings his favorite bedtime song. 

00:00:18.111 --> 00:00:20.479
He turns on his night-light.

00:00:20.573 --> 00:00:23.384
Then — he hears a sound... 

00:00:23.639 --> 00:00:25.828
Tap! … Tap!

00:00:26.676 --> 00:00:29.839
"What’s that sound?” he whispers.

00:00:29.943 --> 00:00:31.943
Tap! … Tap!

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.781
"That sound… it’s coming 
from outside the window!”  

00:00:38.281 --> 00:00:40.157
He climbs out of bed.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.000
He grabs a baseball bat

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.575
and tip-toes towards the window.

00:00:45.392 --> 00:00:48.947
Tappity-tap! TAP!

00:00:48.947 --> 00:00:51.692
“It’s a monster!” he thinks.

00:00:51.815 --> 00:00:56.437
He grabs his bicycle helmet and 
puts it on his head for protection.

00:00:56.635 --> 00:00:58.785
He hears the sound again...

00:00:59.615 --> 00:01:03.307
TAP! ... TAP! … Tappity-TAP!

00:01:03.373 --> 00:01:04.872
Lion panics. 

00:01:04.919 --> 00:01:07.051
“The monster is getting closer!

00:01:07.098 --> 00:01:11.876
It sounds like the BIGGEST, 
SCARIEST monster ever!”

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.602
Tap! ... Tap! ... Tappity-tap!

00:01:14.602 --> 00:01:15.848
TAPPITY-TAP!

00:01:15.905 --> 00:01:18.061
TAPPITY-TAPPITY-TAPPITY…. TAP! 

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:20.031
"EEEK!" Lion squeals.

00:01:20.295 --> 00:01:24.238
He runs away from the window 
and hides under the bed.

00:01:24.511 --> 00:01:27.379
He pulls a blanket over his head.

00:01:27.464 --> 00:01:32.241
He holds his baseball bat tightly 
in his hands, and….

00:01:32.354 --> 00:01:33.864
Tappity tap!

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.508
... A little frog jumps up on the window sill.

00:01:37.781 --> 00:01:41.867
The frog is wearing a tutu and tap shoes.

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:44.130
She dances a little dance.

00:01:44.214 --> 00:01:46.189
Tap tap tappity tap!

00:01:46.525 --> 00:01:50.665
"Hello Lion! Are you in there?” says the frog.

00:01:50.905 --> 00:01:52.752
She looks through the window

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.706
and sees Lion hiding under the bed.

00:01:56.252 --> 00:01:58.641
Lion is wrapped in a blanket…  

00:01:58.641 --> 00:02:00.615
wearing a bicycle helmet … 

00:02:00.615 --> 00:02:03.067
... and holding a baseball bat.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.621
He looks ridiculous. 

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.845
(And to be honest, he feels ridiculous too.)

00:02:10.153 --> 00:02:15.282
"Ummm… I have some new dance moves 
to show you," says the frog. 

00:02:15.559 --> 00:02:17.559
"But you look busy.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.599
I will come back later. See ya!"

00:02:20.925 --> 00:02:25.309
The frog hops down to the ground 
and happily dances away.

00:02:25.449 --> 00:02:27.939
Tap-TAP! Tappity-tappity-TAP!

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:31.210
Moral:

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:36.335
Sometimes our imaginations make 
things scarier than they really are.

